      "notes": "CADRE is a political satire set in a fictional authoritarian state. It contains\r\nno graphic imagery: everything is presented as official documents, reports and\r\npublic broadcasts. The mature content is in what those documents describe.\r\n\r\nRecurring subject matter includes:\r\n\r\n- Famine, and the falsification of records that conceals it\r\n- Political purges \u2014 colleagues can be investigated, reassigned, or removed\r\n  without process, and can be erased from the historical record entirely\r\n- Suppression of civilian unrest, including martial law imposed on regions\r\n  defined by ethnicity and religion\r\n- War, with casualties reported to the player as quarterly figures\r\n- Corruption, surveillance, espionage and bribery\r\n\r\nThe game's method is to describe these things in the cheerful, euphemistic\r\nlanguage of an institution that never admits anything is wrong. Some players\r\nmay find that tone more uncomfortable than explicit depiction would be.\r\n\r\nThere is no sexual content or nudity. There is no depiction of self-harm or\r\nsuicide. Alcohol is referred to once, in passing. No real country, organisation\r\nor person is named."
